  "behavior": [
    "MessageList installs the language closure directly through the native owned renderer slot. Zero falls back, positive completes custom painting, negative status and language exception propagate checked.",
    "The native renderer path holds the callback while invoking it. Self-unregister works; failing registration preserves the previous closure.",
    "A node is exposed as a read-only callback view together with callback-only sender and draw views. Saved views fail once the invocation ends. Explicit text copies survive unregistration.",
    "Reentrant message text modification fails with Busy during paint. Event callback node text is a separate native lifetime contract and is not exposed by this change.",
    "The 50-frame warm comparison uses the same CPU renderer and native paint command, reads only node type and omits saved views and text snapshots. Both C and xlang show 150 allocations, 150 frees and zero reallocations for the complete warmed render loop. No CPU latency claim is made."
  ],
